{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310825,"nonce":"hyxdbVMZWMWY0c3GPsSqLd9ZZKI=","title":"Split compiler into compiler-frontend / compiler-codegen — measured: the cut is already one-way except ONE function","message":"DIRECTION chosen by the owner 2026-08-15, over the cheaper alternative of\nmoving runtime API into `rayzor-runtime-core`: *\"I think having a\ncompiler-frontend and compiler-codegen crate is better.\"* The crate boundary\nmakes the rule enforceable — lowering CANNOT reach a backend — instead of\nrelocating a dependency, and it makes `--no-default-features` mean what it says.\n\n**THE CUT IS ALMOST ALREADY CLEAN — measured, not assumed:**\n- `codegen` -\u003e `ir`/`tast`: 13 files. Expected, one-way.\n- `ir`/`tast`/`stdlib` -\u003e `codegen`: **3 files, and exactly ONE symbol**:\n  `crate::codegen::wgsl_transpiler::transpile_shader_from_hir`, 6 call sites in\n  `ir/mir/expr/call/{mod,shader,native_struct}.rs`.\n\nThat function takes HIR and emits WGSL text — source-to-source lowering, not\nmachine code generation — so **moving `wgsl_transpiler` to the front end\nremoves the only back-edge.** No trait inversion or callback needed.\n\nMODULE SIZES (compiler/src): tast 61,957 / 83 files · ir 74,567 / 112 ·\ncodegen 44,292 / 19 · stdlib 16,628 / 21 · semantic_graph 25,481 / 29 ·\ntools 467 / 3. Top-level: compilation.rs, pipeline*.rs, compiler_plugin.rs,\ndependency_graph.rs, error_codes.rs, hxml.rs, logging.rs.\n\nPROPOSED SHAPE:\n- `compiler-frontend`: tast + ir + stdlib + wgsl_transpiler (+ semantic_graph,\n  which is not built on the CLI path). **No `rayzor-runtime`** — every\n  front-end mention of it is a STRING LITERAL (`\"rayzor_runtime\"`,\n  `\"rayzor_runtime_CC\"`, `\"rayzor_runtime_keep_me\"`), a symbol/library name for\n  later linking, never a Rust call.\n- `compiler-codegen`: the 4 backends + `mir_interpreter` + `tools/aot_build`.\n  Keeps `rayzor-runtime` (features `tcc-runtime`). Real API used, all\n  execution-side: `haxe_sys::haxe_trace_*`, `haxe_string::HaxeString`,\n  `type_system::{register_class_from_mir, register_enum_from_mir, ParamType}`,\n  `plugin_impl::get_plugin`, `concurrency::{rayzor_jit_cleanup,\n  rayzor_wait_all_threads}`. NOTE `aot_compiler.rs` and `c_backend.rs` use\n  ZERO of it — they emit code rather than run it.\n- `compilation.rs` (the driver) needs both; keep it in a thin top crate.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS BEYOND TIDINESS: `rayzor-runtime` is\n`crate-type = [\"cdylib\", \"rlib\", \"staticlib\"]`. The **cdylib** emits a\nfixed-name `librayzor_runtime.dylib`, so ANY build-dependency path to\n`compiler` puts it in the host graph beside the target graph's copy — \"output\nfilename collision\" — and the thin-LTO link then fails with `Can't find section\n__bitcode`. `[profile.release.build-override]` cannot carry `lto`, so there is\nno flag-level escape. With the split, a build script depending only on\n`compiler-frontend` never pulls the cdylib, and `snapshot-gen` could collapse\nback into a build script (see\n[[project_stdlib_snapshot_embed_via_cli_buildrs]]).\n\nSEQUENCING: do [[project_ast_lowering_modularization_chore]] FIRST —\nast_lowering.rs (17,501 lines) sits squarely in the front-end half, and\nsplitting the crate first means moving it twice. Follow the extraction recipe\nand traps in [[project_mir_lowering_modularization]]: pure moves, no behaviour\nchange, and **diff the function-name set** before/after (a whole method\nvanished silently in one past extraction; brace counting lies).\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `project_compiler_frontend_codegen_split` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}